      "narrative": "Maricopa County’s median sale price was essentially flat year over year at $499,990 in August 2026, while the average sale price rose 6.1% to $686,706.[3] Inventory held at 3.6 months, but buyer activity weakened sharply: pending sales fell 34.2% year over year, while new listings declined 8.5% and closed sales declined 4.9%.[3] The combination of fewer listings and a steeper drop in pending sales indicates less competition among buyers and a market with reduced transaction volume rather than clear seller leverage.[3] Construction was mixed in the broader Phoenix market: total housing permits rose 14.2% year over year in June, while single-family permits fell 2.6%.[11]",
